<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_FoundryFloor_TenderSpawn.xml       UtinniPatches · FORGE_MECHANICS_1 F4
  ============================================================================
  forge_kit_spec.md F4: "the glowing tenders as the garrison... Tender kinds
  are mechanoid-family, roster/faction pass; their strings reveal nothing
  (ban #2)." This item's own task brief: "use an EXISTING shipped mechanoid
  PawnKindDef as a clearly-commented PLACEHOLDER, do not invent tender
  content."

  Placeholder kind: vanilla Mech_Pikeman (Biotech). Chosen for zero new
  strings — every label/description a player can see comes straight from
  vanilla's own mechanoid flavor text ("pikeman"), which says nothing about
  the Forge, the towers, or what these things actually run below. Ban #2
  check for this file: no label, description, letter or quest string
  anywhere in this def or its GenStepDef names what the tenders are running
  — the placeholder is a bare cross-reference to an unmodified vanilla
  PawnKindDef, nothing here writes new text about it at all.

  Placed via RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces / RM_SetPieceElement_AnchoredPawn
  (RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards, MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M6 build, read in
  full before writing this) — faction is always null on that element
  ("true wildlife... zero biome wild-spawn commonality; the GenStep is
  their only entry"), the SAME accepted placeholder-wiring shape its own
  header already documents for exactly this case ("a placeholder PawnKindDef
  wired in ahead of the roster pass... does not carry
  RM_CompTerritorialAnchor... EXPECTED, not a bug"). Real tender
  faction/hostility/AI behaviour is roster/faction-pass work, explicitly not
  this kit's job per the spec's own line — owed.

  spotMustBeStandable true — hard-ban-#1 guard (forge_kit_spec.md: "no
  PawnKindDef this kit places may spawn on lava terrain"). This is the ONE
  GenStepDef in this build pass that actually places a PawnKindDef, so this
  field is load-bearing for the ban, not merely tidy: LavaDeep (painted by
  RUT_FoundryFloor_MeltChannels.xml, order 300, before this GenStepDef's own
  850/860) is Impassable and therefore always fails IntVec3.Standable, so a
  tender can never land on the melt.

  count 3 (INVENTED, this pass — "the garrison," no figure named) — a real
  live-tuned figure is owed to a later pass, alongside the roster's own real
  tender kind.

  order 860 — after the salvage cache (850) so tenders spawn with the cache
  sites already reserved (NoNonNaturalEdifices below also guards against
  the reverse case, a cache overlapping an already-placed tender's cell).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_FoundryFloor_TenderSpawn</defName>
    <order>860</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces">
      <count>3</count>
      <spotMustBeStandable>true</spotMustBeStandable>
      <minSpacing>10</minSpacing>
      <minEdgeDistPct>0.05</minEdgeDistPct>
      <warnOnFail>false</warnOnFail>
      <validators>
        <li Class="Verse.ScattererValidator_NoNonNaturalEdifices" />
      </validators>
      <elements>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_SetPieceElement_AnchoredPawn">
          <!-- PLACEHOLDER — roster/faction pass replaces with the real
               tender kind. Vanilla, unmodified; no new string anywhere
               names what it runs (ban #2). -->
          <pawnKind>Mech_Pikeman</pawnKind>
        </li>
      </elements>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
